WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.145
People naturally rely on intuition, experience,

00:00:03.145 --> 00:00:05.340
and mental shortcuts when making decisions.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.480
These approaches can be useful, but they can also introduce blind spots, overconfidence,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.460
and bias.

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.570
Structured analytic techniques provide methods for slowing down thinking,

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.480
challenging assumptions, and making reasoning more transparent.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.320
They help analysts show how they moved from evidence to judgment.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.450
These techniques do not replace expertise.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:25.985
Instead, they help analysts use expertise more effectively when dealing with uncertainty,

00:00:25.985 --> 00:00:27.995
incomplete information, and competing explanations.

00:00:27.995 --> 00:00:29.878
The value of structure is discipline.

00:00:29.878 --> 00:00:33.400
It gives teams repeatable ways to ask better questions, surface uncertainty,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.597
compare possibilities, and communicate judgments with appropriate confidence.
